   $q$In paragraph 2, Lucia decides that a "cursory glance" would not work. The word "cursory" means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"angry or impatient","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"},{"text":"slow and very careful","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"quick and not thorough","is_correct":true},{"text":"written in curving script","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$quick and not thorough$q$, $q$A cursory glance "would tell her almost nothing," so she switches to reading "every letter twice, slowly," which shows cursory means quick and not thorough. "Cursory" may look like "cursive," but the contrast with slow reading is the real clue.$q$, 'draft', '05050e51-5404-579d-af75-41336f95f769')
