   $q$In paragraph 4, scientists test "a striking claim until its limits become clear." Here, "striking" most nearly means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"hitting something with force","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"attracting attention because it is surprising","is_correct":true},{"text":"refusing to work as a protest","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"proven false by later studies","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$attracting attention because it is surprising$q$, $q$The claim refers back to the finding that "drew wide attention" and the popular "forest internet" idea, so striking means surprising and attention-grabbing. The passage says some studies were repeated with similar results, so the claim has not been proven false.$q$, 'draft', 'b93e6386-2a65-58ef-aefe-2334fd66785c')
